    "done_when": "Continue from base f157f8419, which already carries benchmarks/frozen_route_fixed_point_rca.py. The previous attempt's H200 job died at backend initialisation because its script exported JAX_PLATFORMS=gpu, which this JAX resolves to the absent ROCm backend: use JAX_PLATFORMS=cuda. On the H200 (job 1279889, log /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/.reckon-worktrees/nova-a0f1e0938fc2/s21-nova/fsri-frozen-newton-terminal-residual/docs/figures/millisecond-converged-solve/newton-krylov-route/terminal-residual/exact-route-h200.log) the exact-route gate returns residual 2.372871479e-06 against 1e-06 with trajectory residual 7.97e-13, identical to every digit with and without the re-freeze. So the terminal partition did not change, and the frozen map's fixed point is still not a fixed point of the live map. Attempt two (every read live, commit bed0155b) met the residual but ran too slowly to gate. Write docs/figures/millisecond-converged-solve/newton-krylov-route/fixed-point-rca/report.md answering, each with a measured number: (1) whether requalification and re-freeze executed at the terminal state, with the count and the partition difference in cells; (2) at the frozen-Newton terminal state, the live-map residual and the frozen-map residual, decomposed by residual component and by cell, naming the cells and terms that carry the 2.37e-6; (3) every quantity the frozen map holds fixed beyond the topology labels (for example support clip geometry, cut-cell moments, the net-current normalisation lambda, domain masks, operator geometry), with its value at the warmed state against the terminal state; (4) the mechanism, with a falsifiable prediction tested by measurement (for example, refreshing quantity Q at the terminal state and running k more Newton steps drops the live residual below 1e-6); (5) the recommended fix within the locked design, live reads through the warm-up and one partition per Newton pass, with its predicted residual and cost. Run the solves as ONE real H200 job (sbatch with RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1, --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 --mem=64G --time=01:30:00, TMPDIR=/tmp at submit and in the payload, no uv on the compute node, PYTHONPATH at the worktree, pytest --timeout 0 where pytest is used). Write the manifest with a job-id wait_probe and wait_terminal [\\",
